Platform: one-socket Xeon CPU Max 9480 (Sapphire Rapids with on-package HBM) in
HBM flat mode with SNC4: NUMA nodes 0-3 hold the CPUs and the DDR5, nodes 4-7 are
memory-only HBM nodes. No DSA/IAA/QAT work queues or VFs are set up.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- A memory-only node lists an empty cpulist: Documentation/ABI/stable/sysfs-devices-node
  (node<N>/cpulist), drivers/base/node.c.
- SNC: arch/x86/kernel/cpu/resctrl/monitor.c snc_get_config() (CPU 0's L3 CPUs /
  its node's CPUs; SAPPHIRERAPIDS_X is in snc_cpu_ids): 112 / 28 = 4.
- amx_*, rdt_a, cat_l3, cdp_l3, mba: arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeatures.h.
- Balloon memory types DRAM/HBM/PMEM and pinMemory: the bundled nri-plugins
  v0.14.0 CRD (share/nri-balloons.yml, balloonTypes.memoryTypes).

Layout: sysfs paths and relative symlinks follow the driver core's naming, in
exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the matrix test re-captures each
tree and requires an identical result).

Not from hardware: the core count and CPU numbering (56 cores, siblings +56), the
HBM node numbers, the brand string in model name, the kernel release string and the
cpuinfo flags line (the xeon-spr-accel subset).
